  "details": "I'm working with a friend and we're both consistently reproducing an issue where the reported angle of a physbone seems to \"flicker\" to different values. https://i.imgur.com/9p1g43X.mp4\nThis behavior goes away when every object in the hierarchy is scaled to (1,1,1)\n\nI've created a sample scene that demonstrates this behavior (obviously requires VRCSDK)\nhttps://www.dropbox.com/s/fkizr9870gvl65x/FlickerBone.unitypackage?dl=0\n\n* Press play\n* Rotate the TestBoneThing object to any orientation\n* Watch the `FlickerAngle_Angle` parameter.\n\nFor one, it seems like `FlickerAngle_Angle` should be 0 when the bone is at rest, since there is no gravity applied. But if you watch the number, it will actually occasionally flicker to 0 for just a moment. We have also seen it work in reverse, where the bone angle is properly at 0 at rest, but then flickers to a different value, despite the bone not moving.\n\nIf you set the `Armature` object scale to `(1,1,1)` the problem goes away.",
